# Cross-link conventions

normix has two doc trees:

- `docs/` — published Sphinx website (public-facing)
- `dev-notes/` — agent/dev-internal, NOT built or published

## In `docs/**` (published)

- NEVER link to `dev-notes/`. The website cannot resolve those paths.
- Cross-reference other `docs/` pages via MyST `{doc}` or `{ref}` roles, not
  raw relative paths (so Sphinx can validate the link).
- Cross-reference `normix.*` symbols via `{py:class}`, `{py:func}`, `{py:meth}`.
- External URLs are fine; the linkcheck builder validates them in CI.

## Citations (academic / technical)

Canonical bibliography: `docs/references.md` (MyST `(key)=` targets).
Cite with `{ref}`Key <key>`` — never redefine entries on content pages.

**Cite when prose names** a paper, algorithm origin, asymptotic expansion,
special-function identity, or foundational distribution result. Examples:

- Hankel / Olver / small-$z$ Bessel regimes → `{ref}`DLMF <dlmf>`` + section URL
  (e.g. https://dlmf.nist.gov/10.40.E2); quadrature → Takekawa2022
- GIG Devroye TDR / PINV → Devroye2014 / HormannLeydold2011
- EM / online EM / MCECM → Dempster1977 / Cappe2009 / MengRubin1993
- GH / NIG / VG → BarndorffNielsen1977 / 1997 / MadanSeneta1990
- Coherent risk / CVaR / ENB → Artzner1999 / RockafellarUryasev2000 / Meucci*

**Do / don't**

- DO add a new `(key)=` entry to `docs/references.md` when introducing a source
- DO match wording to the implementation (e.g. Devroye is TDR, not ratio-of-uniforms;
  MCECM is Multi-Cycle ECM, not Monte Carlo)
- DON'T leave named expansions bare ("Hankel asymptotic…") without a cite/link
- DON'T invent bibliography keys that aren't in `references.md`

## External packages

In published prose (install table, design rationale, tutorial intros), link the
first meaningful mention of a dependency to its docs. Canonical URLs:

| Package | URL |
|---|---|
| JAX | https://docs.jax.dev/en/latest/ |
| Equinox | https://docs.kidger.site/equinox/ |
| JAXopt | https://jaxopt.github.io/stable/ |
| NumPy | https://numpy.org/doc/stable/ |
| SciPy | https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/ |
| matplotlib | https://matplotlib.org/stable/ |

Don't hyperlink every `import jax` in code cells. Keep dependency tables in
`docs/getting_started/install.md` aligned with `pyproject.toml`.

## In `dev-notes/**` (internal)

- May link freely to `docs/`, other `dev-notes/`, and source code paths.
- Use relative paths (e.g. `../design/em_framework.md`) for IDE preview.
- Do not direct end-users into `dev-notes/` from any public surface.

## In `normix/**/*.py` (docstrings → autodoc → public website)

- Reference public docs via Sphinx `:doc:` or `:ref:` roles, not relative paths.
- NEVER reference `dev-notes/` paths — they are not in the autodoc output.
- Do not link to internal-only locations (`plans/`, `tech_notes/`, etc.).

## In `README.md` and `AGENTS.md`

- `README.md` is for users: link to the published site or `docs/`, not
  `dev-notes/`.
- `AGENTS.md` is for agents: may link to `dev-notes/` freely.

## When moving docs

After structural changes, run `scripts/check_doc_links.sh` and fix any
broken references before merging.
